Jim Strathmeyer wrote:
>
> So I'm in sokoban and find a giant mimic in a boulder when I try to move
> it. It grabes me, and my Archon refuses to attack it. Any ideas why?

I *suspect* that pets will only attack monsters not already involved
in combat.  Grabbing counts as combat.  I believe this is because
coding more than two creatures in a single combat session would be far
too complex for too little gain.

If you manage to break away your Archon will very like go after it.
But mimics rarely survive their prey breaking away.  The standard
method to break their grip is killing them.

